                "event": "Flood Watch",
                "sender": "w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov",
                "senderName": "NWS Flagstaff AZ",
                "headline": "Flood Watch issued October 12 at 12:31AM MST until October 12 at 5:00PM MST by NWS Flagstaff AZ",
                "description": "* WHAT...Flash flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues to be\npossible.\n\n* WHERE...western Coconino, northern Gila, far southern Navajo, and\nYavapai counties.\n\n* WHEN...Through this afternoon.\n\n* IMPACTS...Flash flooding will be possible in creeks, normally dry\nwashes, swimming holes, and over recently burned areas. Raging\nkiller currents will be possible in side canyons and narrow slot\ncanyons. Low-water crossings may be flooded.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Scattered to numerous showers and thunderstorms are expected to\ncontinue across the are through tonight. With tropical moisture\nin place from the remnants of Tropical Storm Rachel and already\nsaturated grounds, periods of embedded heavy rainfall will be\npossible which could lead to flash flooding. Additionally, the\nextended period of rain could lead to elevated flow in creeks,\nnormally dry washes, and rivers.\n- Additional information is available at weather.gov/flagstaff.",
                "instruction": "Have a way to receive Flash Flood Warnings and be prepared to take\naction should warnings be issued.",
                "response": "Prepare",
                "note": null,
