                "headline": "Flood Watch issued October 11 at 7:26PM MDT until October 12 at 6:00PM MDT by NWS Pocatello ID",
                "description": "* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues to be\npossible.\n\n* WHERE...Portions of central, eastern, south central, and southeast\nIdaho, including the following areas, in central Idaho, Sun Valley\nRegion and Wood River Foothills. In eastern Idaho, Beaverhead -\nLemhi Highlands, Big Hole Mountains, Centennial Mountains - Island\nPark and Teton Valley. In south central Idaho, Eastern Magic Valley\nand Shoshone/Lava Beds. In southeast Idaho, Arco/Mud Lake Desert,\nBear Lake Valley, Bear River Range, Blackfoot Mountains, Caribou\nRange, Franklin/Eastern Oneida Region, Lower Snake River Plain,\nMarsh and Arbon Highlands, Raft River Region, Southern Hills/Albion\nMountains and Upper Snake River Plain.\n\n* WHEN...Through Monday afternoon.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, and other low-lying and flood-prone locations.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- A prolonged period of rainfall could lead to some flooding across\nparts of the advised area. An upper low moving into the Pacific\nNorthwest will combine with tropical moisture from Tropical\nCyclone Rachel to usher in a cooler, wetter weather pattern\nacross eastern Idaho.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood",
                "instruction": "You should monitor later forecasts and be alert for possible Flood\nWarnings. Those living in areas prone to flooding should be prepared\nto take action should flooding develop.",
