                "senderName": "NWS Elko NV",
                "headline": "Flood Watch issued October 11 at 4:33PM PDT until October 12 at 5:00AM PDT by NWS Elko NV",
                "description": "* WHAT...Flash flooding and debris flows caused by excessive rainfall\ncontinue to be possible.\n\n* WHERE...Portions of eastern, northeast, and south central Nevada,\nincluding the following areas, in eastern Nevada, White Pine. In\nnortheast Nevada, the Ruby Mountains and East Humboldt Range in\nElko, South Central Elko and Southeastern Elko. In south central\nNevada, Northeastern Nye and Northwestern Nye.\n\n* WHEN...Through 5 am PDT.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, and other low-lying and flood-prone locations.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Deep moisture from decaying Hurricane Rachel continues to move\nnorthward, impacting portions of east-central and eastern Nevada\nthrough roughly Monday. This significant moisture will interact\nwith upper level low pressure to bring widespread showers with\nisolated thunderstorms to the watch area. Moderate to locally\nheavy rain will cause excessive runoff and may result in rock,\nmud, and debris flows in and near former fire burned areas, steep\nterrain, and poorly drained urban areas.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood",
                "instruction": "You should monitor later forecasts and be prepared to take action\nshould Flash Flood Warnings be issued.",
